USCSandbox: write the last variant's keywords on its #else line.

The last vertex and fragment variant of a pass is written as a bare #else, so its keyword set
was lost. tools/shader_gen/generate.py reads every variant's keywords to rebuild the chain.
Output: '#else // KW_A && KW_B // PASS:DX11PixelSM40' (still valid HLSL).

Licence: GPL-3.0, like USCSandbox (https://github.com/nesrak1/USCSandbox).

diff --git a/USCSandbox/Processor/ShaderProcessor.cs b/USCSandbox/Processor/ShaderProcessor.cs
index 2108c20..b80f5bb 100644
--- a/USCSandbox/Processor/ShaderProcessor.cs
+++ b/USCSandbox/Processor/ShaderProcessor.cs
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@ namespace USCSandbox.Processor
                 {
                     structSb.AppendLine();
                     structSb.Append(new string(' ', depth * 4));
-                    structSb.Append("#else");
+                    // keep the last variant's keywords: a generator reading this output needs them
+                    structSb.Append($"#else // {string.Join(" && ", keywords)} // {passName}:{programType}");
                 }
                 else if ((!noVertexVariants && programType == ShaderGpuProgramType.DX11VertexSM40)
                         || (!noFragmentVariants && programType == ShaderGpuProgramType.DX11PixelSM40))
